The number system shown contains a region which has measure incommensurable with the space of real numbers over the field of rational numbers.  The region has finite area. Adequate construction, such as ruler and compasses, is both required.

Note this has been generalized to three dimensions to \emph{Commutative Algebra and Counterexamples}.  A related geometric argument appears in \emph{The Geometric Logic of Boolean Functions}, where the construction is footed by the cube of the affine plane.
